`nativeTestCompile`: Native Image reports that `org.apache.sshd.common.file.root.RootedFileSystemProvider` is stored in the image heap while runtime-initialized. This occurs even with only the scaffold placeholder test, indicating a classpath/service-provider initialization problem rather than a particular generated test. Six later Gradle runs reproduce it. A transient JVM failure parsing `PT10S` occurred earlier but was not the terminal blocker.\n\nAfter 12 iterations, metrics recorded the same starting and ending commit, `0` generated LOC, `0` metadata entries, and unavailable dynamic-access coverage. The preserved test remains a placeholder and the metadata file is empty.\n\nInspect:\n- `logs/org.apache.sshd:sshd-core:2.18.0/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-10T05-38-12-634414Z.log`\n- `logs/org.apache.sshd:sshd-core:2.18.0/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-09-10T06-02-46-433546Z.log`\n- `logs/org.apache.sshd:sshd-core:2.18.0/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-09-10T05-57-55-024343Z.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n1. Reproduce with `./gradlew nativeTestCompile -Pcoordinates=org.apache.sshd:sshd-core:2.18.0 --stacktrace` and trace the `RootedFileSystemProvider` instantiation.\n2. Find a dependency, upstream, or harness-level solution that avoids image-heap capture without adding forbidden build-time-initialization configuration.\n3. Replace the placeholder with meaningful in-process SSH client/server coverage, then rerun the coordinate tests and metadata/coverage generation.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cb174d49cab5cd0016aa248d9703087d294e6bbba265dd6bd\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 24224, "output": 987, "cacheRead": 109696, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 516, "totalTokens": 134907, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1789020357616, "responseId": "resp_0cb174d49cab5cd001